WEBVTT

00:10.135 --> 00:12.137
[theme music]

00:12.762 --> 00:15.765
[squelching]

00:26.943 --> 00:29.946
[all snarling]

00:33.033 --> 00:34.993
[growling]

00:36.578 --> 00:38.329
-Mom.
-[On-jo] Cheong-san, no.

00:45.545 --> 00:46.755
What the hell?

00:51.593 --> 00:52.927
-Damn it!
-[growls]

00:53.011 --> 00:54.179
[grunts]

00:54.929 --> 00:56.097
[grunts]

00:57.766 --> 00:59.225
[Dae-su] There's another zombie here!

00:59.893 --> 01:02.729
[Dae-su grunting]

01:03.646 --> 01:04.647
[Joon-yeong] Dae-su!

01:05.982 --> 01:06.900
Stop it.

01:08.902 --> 01:09.903
Dae-su! Get up!

01:13.907 --> 01:15.617
I said stop that!

01:17.327 --> 01:19.162
-[Cheong-san grunts]
-[growls]

01:21.539 --> 01:23.792
-Stop that!
-Hey!

01:23.875 --> 01:26.836
-[grunts]
-[Joon-yeong] Cheong-san! What the hell?

01:26.920 --> 01:28.296
[thumping continues]

01:28.880 --> 01:30.507
You son of a bitch!

01:30.590 --> 01:32.342
[growling]

01:32.425 --> 01:33.718
[snarling]

01:33.802 --> 01:35.637
[grunting continues]

01:40.308 --> 01:41.434
Stop it!

01:47.065 --> 01:48.066
Let go!

01:48.942 --> 01:50.610
Get the fuck off me!

01:52.904 --> 01:53.905
Mom!

01:53.988 --> 01:56.199
[Cheong-san sobbing]

01:58.118 --> 02:00.036
Mom…
[cries]

02:00.120 --> 02:02.372
[thunder rumbles]

02:02.455 --> 02:04.457
[growling]

02:07.585 --> 02:10.421
[thunder rumbles]

02:10.505 --> 02:12.006
[snarling]

02:21.141 --> 02:23.184
[growling]

02:24.769 --> 02:25.895
Hurry.

02:27.355 --> 02:28.523
Run!

02:28.606 --> 02:30.150
[Wu-jin] Hey, let's go.

02:30.233 --> 02:31.359
Hurry up!

02:31.442 --> 02:32.485
Let's go.

02:32.569 --> 02:33.695
[growls]

02:38.658 --> 02:39.993
Let's go, Cheong-san.

02:42.203 --> 02:43.788
Pull yourself together, man!

02:43.872 --> 02:46.040
[thunder rumbles]

02:46.833 --> 02:48.168
Where are the others?

02:48.751 --> 02:49.586
What?

02:49.669 --> 02:51.129
[Joon-yeong] Where are they?

02:51.713 --> 02:53.464
-[Joon-yeong] What now?
-Did you see them coming?

02:53.548 --> 02:54.841
[snarls]

02:57.302 --> 02:58.469
Cheong-san, please.

02:58.553 --> 03:00.597
-Come with us.
-Let's go.

03:09.772 --> 03:12.942
-[thunder rumbling]
-[groaning]

03:19.741 --> 03:21.743
[somber music]

03:27.081 --> 03:29.334
[growling]

03:34.756 --> 03:36.090
Mom!

03:41.179 --> 03:43.014
Mom!

03:44.140 --> 03:46.142
[somber music continues]

04:06.037 --> 04:08.539
[growling]

04:17.215 --> 04:18.132
Mom…

04:18.716 --> 04:20.301
They're here. Hurry up!

04:20.385 --> 04:21.719
[clanks]

04:21.803 --> 04:22.971
-Wu-jin!
-[Hyo-ryeong] Get up.

04:23.054 --> 04:25.515
Come on. We have to go. Let's go!

04:25.598 --> 04:26.933
[all panting]

04:30.395 --> 04:33.231
-[thunder rumbling]
-[growling]

04:36.192 --> 04:38.069
[lightning crackles]

04:38.152 --> 04:40.154
[all snarling]

04:48.538 --> 04:50.790
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

04:50.873 --> 04:52.458
Shut up. You're so heavy.

04:52.542 --> 04:55.169
[crying]
Mi-jin. Thank you so much.

04:56.963 --> 04:58.798
-Will you go out with me?
-No.

04:58.881 --> 05:00.049
Screw you.

05:00.675 --> 05:01.801
Hold on.

05:01.884 --> 05:03.511
[Joon-seong groans]

05:04.345 --> 05:06.347
-Why? What is it?
-Shh.

05:24.073 --> 05:24.949
Hear that?

05:26.326 --> 05:28.828
Those goddamn fucking zombies. Shit.

05:30.997 --> 05:31.831
Let's go.

05:35.918 --> 05:36.836
Let's run.

05:36.919 --> 05:37.795
To the mountain.

05:42.675 --> 05:43.676
Aah!

05:43.760 --> 05:45.970
[zombies snarling]

05:50.850 --> 05:52.769
Ji-min. Help me.

05:52.852 --> 05:54.145
[breathes heavily]

05:54.228 --> 05:56.439
[zombie snarling]

06:04.238 --> 06:05.156
[Wu-jin] Hyo-ryeong!

06:06.532 --> 06:08.284
-[growls]
-[yelps]

06:11.245 --> 06:12.163
[Wu-jin] Get up!

06:15.541 --> 06:16.584
[yelps]

06:19.253 --> 06:20.713
[zombie snarling]

06:22.215 --> 06:23.966
[thunder rumbles]

06:27.929 --> 06:28.846
Get up.

06:28.930 --> 06:30.807
[whimpers]

06:35.853 --> 06:36.687
Sister.

06:37.563 --> 06:39.565
[hopeful music]

06:56.040 --> 06:57.375
[whimpers]

06:58.251 --> 06:59.961
[growling]

07:00.878 --> 07:01.796
[yelps]

07:06.300 --> 07:09.303
[whimpering]

07:16.269 --> 07:17.812
-Wu-jin.
-What are you doing here?

07:17.895 --> 07:18.855
Come on.

07:18.938 --> 07:19.939
Get going.

07:24.110 --> 07:25.862
-Hey!
-Hyo-ryeong. You go first.

07:26.946 --> 07:29.115
-Come on! Let's go!
-Let's go.

07:39.500 --> 07:42.336
[all panting]

07:47.842 --> 07:48.843
What's wrong, Nam-ra?

07:51.220 --> 07:52.305
Run.

07:54.765 --> 07:55.850
Let's go.

07:57.727 --> 07:59.604
[thunder rumbles]

07:59.687 --> 08:01.314
Oh, shit.

08:02.064 --> 08:03.024
[Su-hyeok] Run!

08:03.900 --> 08:05.818
I'm gonna die tonight!

08:05.902 --> 08:07.987
-Run! Go!
-Just save yourselves!

08:08.488 --> 08:10.865
Just go! You'll die! Believe me!

08:10.948 --> 08:12.867
Whatever!
[grunts]

08:13.576 --> 08:15.620
-Over here!
-This way! Hurry!

08:15.703 --> 08:16.662
Come on!

08:25.671 --> 08:27.632
[Joon-seong] Are you crazy? Let go!

08:27.715 --> 08:30.218
[grunting]

08:32.178 --> 08:34.597
Hey! No! No!

08:35.431 --> 08:36.557
[screams]
No!

08:36.641 --> 08:37.642
What are you doing?

08:37.725 --> 08:40.228
[Mi-jin] No! Let go of me, you assholes!

08:40.311 --> 08:41.729
Let me go!

08:41.812 --> 08:43.898
-[Joon-seong screams]
-Let go off me! No!

08:43.981 --> 08:45.900
Get out of here! Hurry!

08:47.026 --> 08:50.905
No! Joon-seong! Joon-seong…

08:50.988 --> 08:53.282
[Joon-seong screaming]

08:53.366 --> 08:55.034
Joon-seong!
[crying]

08:56.744 --> 08:58.538
[Mi-jin] No! Let me go!

08:58.621 --> 09:00.748
[growling]

09:00.831 --> 09:02.875
[screaming]

09:04.627 --> 09:05.878
Shit.

09:13.511 --> 09:14.679
Damn it.

09:18.391 --> 09:21.769
[sobbing]

09:26.566 --> 09:29.277
[breathes shakily]

09:31.112 --> 09:34.073
[Mi-jin sobbing]

09:40.162 --> 09:43.040
[mellow music]

10:12.153 --> 10:13.904
Hey, Cheong-san, I'm…

10:18.159 --> 10:19.201
so sorry.

10:20.620 --> 10:22.496
I didn't know she was your mom.

10:27.918 --> 10:28.794
I'm sorry.

10:33.174 --> 10:35.009
[clatters]

10:36.010 --> 10:38.012
[somber music]

10:59.241 --> 11:00.368
I'm sorry.

11:00.451 --> 11:02.411
[sobbing]

11:17.385 --> 11:18.344
Stop!

11:18.427 --> 11:19.970
-[crying]
-[snarls]

11:23.682 --> 11:24.892
Don't do this.

11:24.975 --> 11:27.978
[growling]

11:29.021 --> 11:31.023
No!
[screaming]

11:43.661 --> 11:46.997
[crying]

11:49.959 --> 11:51.710
Mommy…

11:51.794 --> 11:53.671
[crying]

12:02.596 --> 12:03.681
[growls]

12:12.982 --> 12:14.984
[thunder rumbles]

12:18.529 --> 12:20.531
[Byeong-chan] A virus
must have a consistent pattern

12:20.614 --> 12:22.158
for us to create a vaccine.

12:22.241 --> 12:23.742
[growling]

12:23.826 --> 12:25.327
But the Jonas Virus…

12:26.287 --> 12:28.539
transforms and evolves on its own.

12:28.622 --> 12:30.374
[growling]

12:30.458 --> 12:32.543
It is an ever-changing monster.

12:34.211 --> 12:35.796
[growls]

12:36.755 --> 12:38.674
It's impossible to create a vaccine.

12:39.550 --> 12:41.177
There is only one solution.

12:44.972 --> 12:46.056
Slaughter.

12:47.683 --> 12:50.311
Completely burning and killing the host,

12:50.394 --> 12:52.730
so not a single cell remains.

12:54.690 --> 12:58.027
The moment we are consumed by arrogance
and think we can defeat the virus,

12:59.403 --> 13:01.030
humankind will end.

13:05.242 --> 13:07.495
The file was massive,
so we couldn't analyze it all,

13:07.578 --> 13:09.997
but a significant portion
of it is credible, sir.

13:10.789 --> 13:12.416
And where is the proof for that?

13:12.500 --> 13:17.379
Well, KDCA is creating a virus
using the exact method he described.

13:18.964 --> 13:20.508
If they create the same virus,

13:20.591 --> 13:23.344
then the KDCA will conclude it's credible.

13:23.427 --> 13:25.513
[scoffs]
Well…

13:27.348 --> 13:30.017
Many soldiers are going insane
from this thing, but…

13:30.100 --> 13:32.770
It's scarier when a scientist goes crazy.

13:32.853 --> 13:34.772
Did you hear
they're expanding martial law?

13:36.065 --> 13:36.982
Martial law?

13:37.816 --> 13:39.944
Why would they do that
if we're handling it well?

13:40.528 --> 13:42.488
My friend in the NIS analysis team

13:42.571 --> 13:45.658
said they're discussing pulling back
the blockade to Yangdong

13:45.741 --> 13:47.201
and expanding martial law.

13:51.497 --> 13:52.706
What about Hyosan?

13:55.459 --> 13:57.586
I think they're willing
to make sacrifices.

14:01.507 --> 14:03.008
[sighs]

14:06.262 --> 14:08.722
We may have ceased
our rescue operation for now, but…

14:10.182 --> 14:13.060
there might not be another time
to rescue survivors.

14:15.396 --> 14:17.773
Strengthen the blockade
on the outskirts of Hyosan.

14:19.650 --> 14:22.236
The moment the blockade
is penetrated by the infected,

14:24.071 --> 14:25.614
we'll have to step up and…

14:26.991 --> 14:28.492
abandon Hyosan.

14:29.243 --> 14:31.245
[suspenseful music]

14:32.705 --> 14:33.706
[party leader] Take this.

14:40.004 --> 14:41.338
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

14:45.050 --> 14:48.220
Childish to think the party leader
came personally to save me.

14:49.096 --> 14:50.389
You came to dump me.

14:50.472 --> 14:52.516
My NIS source says

14:52.600 --> 14:56.186
something is going to happen very soon
in Hyosan.

14:56.979 --> 15:00.774
In your district.
If something bad really does happen,

15:00.858 --> 15:04.695
I'll say you even resigned from your post
thinking it would help prevent it.

15:04.778 --> 15:07.114
No one would even think of blaming you.

15:07.197 --> 15:08.532
Blame me for what?

15:08.616 --> 15:11.869
Trust me, you're gonna sign it.

15:11.952 --> 15:15.414
I'll protect your political career
until the end.

15:16.916 --> 15:19.543
Do you need time to think it over?

15:19.627 --> 15:21.420
You failed Hyosan.

15:25.466 --> 15:26.634
They'll just abandon it?

15:27.509 --> 15:29.178
Sign it within the day,

15:29.261 --> 15:33.182
and hand it to the person in charge
of this place.

15:33.265 --> 15:34.183
[sighs]

15:37.811 --> 15:39.063
[sighs]

15:43.359 --> 15:44.777
Hmm…

15:49.740 --> 15:51.116
Sir, um, can you hear me?

15:52.034 --> 15:53.786
-[party leader] Let's go.
-Excuse me, sir!

15:53.869 --> 15:55.120
Oh, damn.

15:55.204 --> 15:57.998
Assemblywoman?
You're getting us out now, right?

15:58.082 --> 16:01.585
The party leader came,
so it'll all be resolved very soon, right?

16:02.127 --> 16:05.422
[Dal-ho] He says he'll save us, right?

16:06.048 --> 16:06.966
Ma'am?

16:27.528 --> 16:30.406
[glass shatters]

16:53.762 --> 16:55.764
[birds chirping]

17:46.315 --> 17:47.232
[sighs]

17:51.111 --> 17:52.738
I thought about it all night long.

17:54.656 --> 17:55.824
How do I live?

17:58.118 --> 17:59.244
What do I do?

18:10.130 --> 18:12.007
Why don't we talk about this later?

18:13.675 --> 18:15.636
Tomorrow or the day after.

18:15.719 --> 18:17.012
Or next week, maybe.

18:17.096 --> 18:19.306
[soft music]

18:19.389 --> 18:21.391
Let's get out of here and eat some food,

18:21.934 --> 18:24.144
and shower first, okay?

18:24.228 --> 18:25.395
We'll talk about it then.

18:26.271 --> 18:27.147
Hmm?

18:33.445 --> 18:35.322
We have a lot to talk about, you know?

18:37.574 --> 18:39.243
Let's give it time.

18:47.835 --> 18:49.837
[soft music continues]

18:52.840 --> 18:54.466
Whatever happens…

18:56.385 --> 18:57.511
please don't give up.

19:00.055 --> 19:01.014
Okay?

19:05.727 --> 19:06.603
Okay.

19:16.822 --> 19:17.656
Never.

19:20.784 --> 19:21.660
Mm-hmm.

19:23.120 --> 19:23.954
You too.

19:26.373 --> 19:27.207
Mm-hmm.

19:28.792 --> 19:29.793
It'll be okay.

19:32.004 --> 19:34.006
[suspenseful music]

19:53.275 --> 19:56.111
[panting]

20:00.449 --> 20:01.783
[yelps]

20:03.660 --> 20:05.037
[groaning]

20:13.754 --> 20:15.422
[groans]

20:17.758 --> 20:19.092
[groans]

20:32.648 --> 20:33.523
[Su-hyeok] What is it?

20:34.650 --> 20:35.776
Do you see something?

20:41.406 --> 20:43.325
The smell is stronger.

20:46.411 --> 20:48.413
[sniffs]

20:49.915 --> 20:52.000
[sniffing continues]

20:54.169 --> 20:55.837
I can't really smell anything.

20:57.172 --> 20:59.258
I think they're all coming this way.

20:59.841 --> 21:01.093
The smell is really strong.

21:02.970 --> 21:06.306
Doesn't matter.
We're all trapped in here for good now.

21:07.307 --> 21:08.642
And there's no way to get out.

21:10.394 --> 21:11.728
Please don't say that.

21:12.980 --> 21:13.814
So don't.

21:14.690 --> 21:15.816
I think we're done.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.068
Ah, damn it!

21:18.694 --> 21:20.279
Let them kill us if they want.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.326
[sighs]

21:29.538 --> 21:31.164
-[Wu-jin] Ha-ri.
-[exhales deeply]

21:32.082 --> 21:35.085
[Wu-jin] You didn't fail
in the preliminaries, did you?

21:37.546 --> 21:38.380
No.

21:39.589 --> 21:40.674
I did really well.

21:42.050 --> 21:43.218
Your tournament.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.013
What happened?
Why did you come to the school?

21:50.267 --> 21:52.978
-You're her brother?
-Yeah, I am.

21:53.061 --> 21:55.856
She got a perfect score,
so she made it to nationals.

21:55.939 --> 21:56.773
I saw her.

21:59.192 --> 22:00.027
Really?

22:01.903 --> 22:03.322
Mm-hmm. It's true.

22:04.239 --> 22:06.867
No way. Really?
You're really in the nationals?

22:07.659 --> 22:08.618
Mom and Dad don't know?

22:08.702 --> 22:11.121
[scoffs]
Bro, how could they now? Look around.

22:11.204 --> 22:14.374
She jumped out of archery bus
and ran to the school to find you.

22:14.458 --> 22:15.334
Kid.

22:15.917 --> 22:17.252
You be good to her.

22:19.546 --> 22:20.464
And to me too.

22:25.010 --> 22:26.053
Who is she?

22:27.095 --> 22:28.764
[Wu-jin] Why does she keep
talking for you?

22:32.267 --> 22:33.393
She's my friend.

22:34.478 --> 22:36.730
[chuckles]
Yeah. We're freaking besties.

22:38.690 --> 22:40.150
[gasps]
You scared me.

22:40.901 --> 22:41.943
What's your deal?

22:42.027 --> 22:43.445
[clears throat]

22:45.530 --> 22:46.364
I…

22:47.949 --> 22:49.034
You?

22:51.244 --> 22:52.621
I think you're the perfect girl.

22:52.704 --> 22:54.498
What? You freak.

22:54.581 --> 22:55.791
[quirky music]

22:55.874 --> 22:56.833
Hey.

22:57.751 --> 22:58.919
What's wrong with you?

22:59.002 --> 23:01.755
I watched you
when you were shooting your arrows,

23:01.838 --> 23:03.965
I saw you train every morning.

23:04.883 --> 23:07.094
I went to every tournament
and cheered for you.

23:07.177 --> 23:09.679
Caught myself yelling "copper beauty"
a few times.

23:09.763 --> 23:12.349
I really liked you for many years.

23:14.101 --> 23:14.976
[Dae-su] Now…

23:15.936 --> 23:18.396
I wanna be a man, not just a fan.

23:20.315 --> 23:23.777
I'm gonna die, anyway.
I just wanna say what I want first.

23:34.037 --> 23:34.955
Cool.

23:36.206 --> 23:37.332
You're Dae-su, right?

23:38.041 --> 23:40.127
You call my brother "brother-in-law"?

23:41.419 --> 23:42.295
Yeah.

23:43.171 --> 23:44.548
So that means you knew.

23:45.340 --> 23:46.842
Brother-in-law, you told her?

23:46.925 --> 23:49.469
Yeah, I might have.
[chuckles]

23:54.516 --> 23:55.934
Must be nice to meet me.

23:56.017 --> 23:57.394
Yes.

23:57.477 --> 23:59.396
-Then you're okay with dying?
-Yes.

24:00.355 --> 24:01.314
What? Today?

24:01.398 --> 24:02.691
-[grunts]
-[groans]

24:02.774 --> 24:05.652
Good. I'm pissed off and needed to vent.

24:05.735 --> 24:07.028
Wu-jin, stop her.

24:07.112 --> 24:08.280
-Ha-ri, hey.
-Stop her.

24:08.363 --> 24:11.116
-Come here. Get over here.
-I'm sorry. I was wrong.

24:11.199 --> 24:12.534
[Ha-ri panting]

24:12.617 --> 24:15.245
-No. I'm glad you told me.
-[Dae-su] Hey. No, that's not it.

24:15.328 --> 24:16.913
-Yes, it is. Get over here now.
-No, I…

24:16.997 --> 24:19.416
Why don't you understand?
I really like you.

24:19.499 --> 24:21.501
-Get over here, dear husband.
-[Dae-su] Wu-jin. Hey.

24:21.585 --> 24:23.628
-[Wu-jin] Sorry.
-Stop her, Wu-jin.

24:23.712 --> 24:24.838
-No!
-Beat him up, sis.

24:24.921 --> 24:26.673
Get over here. You punk.

24:26.756 --> 24:29.551
-[Wu-jin] He needs a good beating.
-[Mi-jin] Look at him dodging.

24:29.634 --> 24:31.720
-[Mi-jin laughs]
-[grunts]

24:32.429 --> 24:33.346
What's that?

24:34.639 --> 24:36.057
-[grunts]
-That's not it!

24:37.475 --> 24:38.727
[Dae-su] Guys.

24:38.810 --> 24:42.063
[Ha-ri] Come here. Gonna get you, asshole!

24:42.147 --> 24:45.817
-Hey, hey, stop it. Stop it. Stop her.
-I don't want to come between you two.

24:45.901 --> 24:48.320
-Right now.
-Okay. Only if you promise not to hit me.

24:51.281 --> 24:53.283
[ominous music]

24:54.659 --> 24:55.702
[grunts]

25:07.130 --> 25:10.133
Where did those shitheads run off to now?

25:18.058 --> 25:20.393
[clanking]

25:23.688 --> 25:24.940
[clangs]

25:26.650 --> 25:27.901
What are you doing?

25:27.984 --> 25:30.445
Can we move this?
Do you think it's possible?

25:41.081 --> 25:44.793
We can tie all the carts in a circle,
then we can just use them as a shield.

25:52.300 --> 25:53.551
[Wu-jin] This way.

25:53.635 --> 25:56.346
We need strings or something
to tie them together.

25:57.389 --> 25:59.015
[Mi-jin] Is this it?

25:59.599 --> 26:00.684
[Joon-yeong] This?

26:07.941 --> 26:09.234
Cut as many as possible.

26:10.610 --> 26:14.155
Hey. There's no way this is going to work.

26:14.239 --> 26:17.450
We should flip it over completely,
so that we can hide underneath.

26:17.534 --> 26:19.536
Uh… We should stand it up.

26:19.619 --> 26:21.830
Yeah, zombies sure can't climb that?

26:21.913 --> 26:23.331
[sighs]
That's enough.

26:23.415 --> 26:25.917
Don't be stupid. Okay? Let's redo them.

26:26.543 --> 26:28.753
It's too short if we close the lids.

26:28.837 --> 26:30.130
Unless you want us crawling?

26:30.213 --> 26:32.007
Pulling rank right now?

26:32.090 --> 26:33.133
-[slams]
-Hey.

26:33.758 --> 26:35.385
Say it to my face!

26:35.468 --> 26:37.012
If you don't like it, make your own.

26:38.013 --> 26:38.930
[scoffs]

26:41.725 --> 26:43.059
There.

26:43.143 --> 26:44.644
Oh, shit. Are you crazy?

26:45.687 --> 26:46.604
What's wrong with you?

26:47.772 --> 26:50.150
-Sis, stop her.
-Come on. Say that again.

26:50.233 --> 26:52.277
Do everyone a favor
and stay out of our way.

26:52.360 --> 26:54.487
Hey, you.
[grunts]

26:54.571 --> 26:56.990
[groans]
Shithead!

26:57.073 --> 26:59.242
"Shithead"? Shithead. What the fuck?

26:59.326 --> 27:00.201
Stop it.

27:00.785 --> 27:02.662
Joon-yeong, you too.

27:02.746 --> 27:04.748
Who the hell is she to tell us
we have to redo it?

27:04.831 --> 27:07.500
"Who the hell is she?"
Your fucking nightmare.

27:07.584 --> 27:10.587
-You're coming with us, right?
-You're the ones coming with me.

27:10.670 --> 27:11.838
[sighs]

27:11.921 --> 27:13.673
You won't just leave them here, right?

27:13.757 --> 27:14.883
I wish, but no.

27:14.966 --> 27:18.136
We're going together, anyway.
Why fight now, huh?

27:18.219 --> 27:20.513
Just do as I say
unless you wanna die out there.

27:20.597 --> 27:21.598
Which you might.

27:21.681 --> 27:23.892
We're tryna make it that high,
so we don't die out there.

27:23.975 --> 27:25.393
Enough already.

27:27.645 --> 27:29.397
How many people have died on our way here?

27:29.981 --> 27:31.441
[Su-hyeok] We can't lose anyone else.

27:32.067 --> 27:34.319
We shouldn't waste energy
fighting among ourselves.

27:34.402 --> 27:35.820
I'm not fighting to die.

27:36.696 --> 27:38.323
I'm fighting because I wanna live.

27:38.406 --> 27:40.992
Then do as I fucking say, asshead.

27:42.452 --> 27:43.912
Unless we split up.

27:43.995 --> 27:45.205
-Problem solved.
-[clangs]

27:46.581 --> 27:48.041
-Get back here. You hear me?
-Joon-yeong.

27:48.124 --> 27:49.250
[Mi-jin] Get back here!

27:49.334 --> 27:50.752
Let go of me, asshole!

27:50.835 --> 27:52.670
You think I'm doing this,
because I wanna die?

27:52.754 --> 27:55.465
[clanging]

27:57.717 --> 27:59.010
We'll vote on it.

27:59.094 --> 28:00.595
[sighs]
You are?

28:02.972 --> 28:03.890
Class prez.

28:06.184 --> 28:07.769
One. Split up.

28:12.273 --> 28:13.691
Two. Stay together.

28:17.028 --> 28:21.157
-Okay, we voted to stay together, then.
-Is it smart to vote

28:21.241 --> 28:23.701
on life and death matters
and just follow the majority?

28:24.494 --> 28:26.996
What if we collectively decide
to do the wrong thing?

28:27.080 --> 28:29.457
You know, there's such a thing
as collective intelligence.

28:29.541 --> 28:31.292
There are too many
unintelligent people here.

28:31.376 --> 28:33.837
You can't make intelligence
with a bunch of idiots.

28:33.920 --> 28:35.422
So then what do you suggest?

28:36.464 --> 28:38.133
Do we vote about voting, huh?

28:38.216 --> 28:41.261
Fuck! How the hell did
your kids survive up to now?

28:41.344 --> 28:43.430
Sorry, but can you mind your own business?

28:43.513 --> 28:45.765
You started the fight, now we're voting.

28:45.849 --> 28:47.475
Give me an arrow, so I can stab him.

28:47.559 --> 28:49.060
Anyway, let's move on now.

28:50.103 --> 28:52.397
One. We make the outside higher.

29:02.657 --> 29:03.491
Five votes.

29:04.075 --> 29:04.951
Two.

29:06.536 --> 29:08.455
We fold the lids, make a box.

29:13.752 --> 29:15.128
So that's four.

29:15.211 --> 29:17.630
What the hell? I thought you were with us?

29:18.882 --> 29:19.841
I changed my mind.

29:20.383 --> 29:24.304
Option one received the majority vote,
so make the walls high.

29:25.430 --> 29:26.723
Wait. Your vote.

29:28.141 --> 29:30.477
If you're for option two, it's a tie.

29:31.936 --> 29:32.812
Option one.

29:32.896 --> 29:34.272
Oh, shit.

29:35.148 --> 29:37.567
Okay. Let's do it.

29:37.650 --> 29:40.820
Okay, but don't resent me
when the zombies climb over

29:40.904 --> 29:42.113
and kill us all.

29:42.614 --> 29:44.908
Don't worry, I'll take the front
and any blame.

29:44.991 --> 29:46.075
You hold back.

29:46.159 --> 29:48.328
Oh, what an asshole. Fuck.

29:48.411 --> 29:50.705
Why are kids so damn rude these days?

29:50.789 --> 29:52.040
And you're not?

29:52.791 --> 29:55.585
Don't say that in front
of the underclassmen.

29:56.461 --> 30:00.673
This is the virus that was created
using Lee Byeong-chan's method precisely.

30:01.257 --> 30:03.760
This is a sample from an infected.

30:03.843 --> 30:07.222
[doctor] The two viruses
are 98 percent match.

30:08.848 --> 30:11.601
Are you saying everything he says
in the videos is true?

30:11.684 --> 30:14.938
Yes. When someone gets infected,
their heart stops.

30:15.021 --> 30:16.439
Only the virus survives.

30:16.523 --> 30:18.942
It stimulates the brainstem
and moves the body.

30:19.025 --> 30:20.777
They're like moving corpses.

30:22.320 --> 30:24.614
We haven't found any way to save the dead.

30:26.950 --> 30:29.494
You're telling me that he's dead?

30:30.578 --> 30:34.290
Staff Sergeant Lee Jae-jun is dead
from a medical perspective.

30:35.542 --> 30:36.960
[doctor] But she's, ugh…

30:37.043 --> 30:38.878
Difficult to explain.

30:40.338 --> 30:42.674
She was found alive.

30:43.925 --> 30:47.971
There has never been a virus with such
a fast rate of infection in history.

30:48.054 --> 30:50.807
Our only solution
is getting rid of the host.

30:50.890 --> 30:54.060
I'm not going to tolerate
the sign of indifference!

30:54.143 --> 30:56.271
Your only job is to find me a cure.

31:00.567 --> 31:01.651
Commander, sir.

31:01.734 --> 31:03.319
They broke through the barricade.

31:03.903 --> 31:05.405
[soldier] It's spreading into Yangdong.

31:07.615 --> 31:08.908
[Seon-moo] How bad is the spread?

31:08.992 --> 31:11.870
[soldier] They're taking route 643
into downtown Yangdong.

31:11.953 --> 31:14.873
We sent army reservists
in the area to the barricades.

31:14.956 --> 31:17.959
[growling]

31:18.918 --> 31:21.921
Send all the reservists to create
a lockdown zone in Yangdong

31:22.005 --> 31:23.339
and evacuate the city.

31:23.423 --> 31:25.133
-Call in all the advisers.
-Yes, sir.

31:26.217 --> 31:28.803
You said you had a friend in the NIS?

31:28.887 --> 31:30.096
Yes.

31:30.179 --> 31:31.890
Ask him to meet officially.

31:31.973 --> 31:32.891
Yes, sir.

31:38.688 --> 31:40.732
[Joon-yeong] You have to tie
the knots harder.

31:41.399 --> 31:42.567
[Hyo-ryeong] Here too?

31:45.528 --> 31:47.071
-[Dae-su] I hope we're not doing…
-[Hyo-ryeong] Can you do it?

31:47.155 --> 31:48.907
-…anything stupid.
-My hands hurt.

31:48.990 --> 31:50.992
-[Wu-jin] Just do it.
-[Dae-su] Hey, that looks good.

31:51.075 --> 31:52.619
Hand it to me. We're gonna die, anyway.

31:52.702 --> 31:54.329
-[Mi-jin] Hey, come here.
-[Hyo-ryeong] Me?

31:54.412 --> 31:57.999
-[Dae-su] I almost got killed confessing…
-Hey. Chocolate bar.

32:01.711 --> 32:02.795
Let me see.

32:04.005 --> 32:05.465
You think we can eat it, huh?

32:07.216 --> 32:08.593
Oh, no, expired.

32:08.676 --> 32:09.928
Okay, so what?

32:11.095 --> 32:12.221
Okay, yeah, you're right.

32:18.269 --> 32:19.729
[wrapping rustling]

32:21.898 --> 32:23.691
Only take a tiny bite.

32:24.776 --> 32:27.236
[Dae-su] It needs to feed all of us. Okay?

32:31.157 --> 32:34.410
Oh, shit. I said a tiny bite.

32:34.494 --> 32:36.829
I only ate freaking this much.

32:36.913 --> 32:39.207
Selfish bastard.

32:43.044 --> 32:44.045
[gulps]

32:51.719 --> 32:52.679
I'm full, so…

33:08.528 --> 33:10.071
Mmm.

33:10.154 --> 33:12.156
[munching]

33:23.251 --> 33:25.169
I really don't want that. Here.

33:30.758 --> 33:32.218
-Hey.
-[Dae-su] What?

33:32.301 --> 33:33.678
Joon-yeong didn't have any.

33:35.555 --> 33:37.098
[Wu-jin] How could you eat it all?

33:40.768 --> 33:41.769
I…

33:42.270 --> 33:45.273
I… I thought I was last. I'm really sorry.

33:46.774 --> 33:50.236
I guess we just… armor up, right?

33:52.905 --> 33:56.325
-That asshole.
-Joon-yeong, you put on the best armor.

33:57.660 --> 33:59.662
[gloomy music]

34:02.040 --> 34:04.625
[grunting]

34:07.045 --> 34:09.088
Take off your shoes
and I'll do yours first.

34:11.049 --> 34:12.300
Just hold on a sec.

34:12.383 --> 34:14.385
[suspenseful music]

34:17.680 --> 34:18.598
Hold on tight.

34:32.945 --> 34:33.780
Hey, Cheong-san.

34:33.863 --> 34:34.947
What?

34:39.869 --> 34:41.079
Do you really hate me?

34:41.162 --> 34:42.330
Mm-mmm.

34:42.413 --> 34:43.372
Why not?

34:43.456 --> 34:44.415
Crazy.

34:45.374 --> 34:46.876
I've never hated you at all.

34:48.211 --> 34:49.378
That amazes me too.

34:56.844 --> 34:58.054
[sighs]

35:02.350 --> 35:04.769
[Mi-jin breathes heavily]

35:09.482 --> 35:10.399
This is it.

35:12.026 --> 35:13.027
Here we go.

35:13.111 --> 35:13.945
Hold on.

35:16.531 --> 35:17.657
This will work?

35:19.367 --> 35:20.284
It will work.

35:21.536 --> 35:24.997
-Just stay next to me, okay?
-You stay next to me.

35:25.581 --> 35:26.749
[Wu-jin] And don't get killed.

35:33.214 --> 35:35.299
You don't want it, so we both can't move.

35:37.593 --> 35:38.886
I'm scared.

35:48.980 --> 35:51.357
I'm gonna take the lead.
You take the back.

35:58.406 --> 35:59.282
Are you ready?

36:00.241 --> 36:01.701
[sighs]
Shit.

36:02.535 --> 36:04.328
You better be right with this.

36:04.412 --> 36:06.455
We've seen so many zombies already.

36:08.541 --> 36:10.626
They're not smart enough for this.

36:22.180 --> 36:24.765
[suspenseful music]

36:26.893 --> 36:29.061
[grunts]
Push!

36:29.145 --> 36:30.229
-Hurry!
-[growling]

36:31.898 --> 36:32.773
Let's go!

36:33.649 --> 36:34.650
More!

36:34.734 --> 36:35.651
Turn!

36:36.402 --> 36:37.236
[Mi-jin] Turn!

36:38.487 --> 36:40.740
-[Joon-yeong] Get in! Get in!
-[Hyo-ryeong screams]

36:41.657 --> 36:43.576
-[grunts]
-[Su-hyeok] Close it!

36:47.121 --> 36:48.581
Did you tie it?

36:49.540 --> 36:50.666
Done! Push!

36:50.750 --> 36:51.626
[Mi-jin] Push!

36:52.126 --> 36:53.169
[snarling]

36:53.252 --> 36:55.046
[all grunting]

36:57.632 --> 36:58.883
Push!

36:58.966 --> 37:00.509
[Dae-su] Damn it!

37:01.427 --> 37:02.845
They're climbing over!

37:03.763 --> 37:05.223
[zombies snarling]

37:06.515 --> 37:07.892
It won't budge!

37:08.684 --> 37:09.644
Push harder!

37:10.311 --> 37:11.312
We can do this!

37:13.773 --> 37:16.317
-[Joon-yeong] Push harder! Harder!
-[Mi-jin] It won't move!

37:20.655 --> 37:23.199
[growling]

37:26.494 --> 37:28.412
[whimpering]

37:29.997 --> 37:32.833
[grunting]

37:44.720 --> 37:46.931
[screaming]

37:51.394 --> 37:53.104
[Su-hyeok] Be careful!

37:53.187 --> 37:54.146
[yelps]

37:55.398 --> 37:56.274
On-jo!

37:56.357 --> 37:58.276
[grunting]

37:59.777 --> 38:01.362
What are you doing? Push!

38:01.445 --> 38:02.947
[grunting]

38:05.950 --> 38:07.952
[suspenseful music]

38:20.006 --> 38:21.424
[sniffs]

38:24.010 --> 38:28.431
-[growling]
-[grunting]

38:30.933 --> 38:33.936
-Su-hyeok! Above you!
-[grunts]

38:35.646 --> 38:37.565
[screaming]

38:38.065 --> 38:38.899
Fuck!

38:41.694 --> 38:44.155
-[crunches]
-[groaning]

38:51.704 --> 38:54.874
[Mi-jin whimpering]
Hey, are you okay?

38:56.792 --> 38:58.252
[Mi-jin] Oh, shit.

38:58.336 --> 39:00.338
[growling]

39:02.006 --> 39:04.258
[grunting]

39:07.511 --> 39:10.848
Shit. I said I'd take responsibility.

39:12.975 --> 39:14.769
-Where are you going?
-Hey, wait!

39:14.852 --> 39:16.896
-Joon-yeong!
-Hey! Hey!

39:16.979 --> 39:18.147
[Dae-su] Joon-yeong!

39:18.230 --> 39:20.149
-Where are you going?
-[Cheong-san] Hey! Don't go!

39:28.240 --> 39:29.116
Get off!

39:29.992 --> 39:31.452
[grumbling]

39:32.495 --> 39:34.663
Push! Push!

39:35.247 --> 39:36.916
[grunting]

39:36.999 --> 39:38.167
Hurry up and push!

39:50.721 --> 39:53.265
[groaning]

39:53.349 --> 39:55.601
[Joon-yeong] Go home! Make it home!

39:55.684 --> 39:58.562
[groans]
Go home!

39:59.688 --> 40:01.524
Make it home!

40:03.317 --> 40:04.610
No! Hey!

40:07.446 --> 40:09.073
-[Mi-jin] Ugh! Joon-seong!
-Keep going!

40:09.615 --> 40:11.283
Keep going!

40:11.909 --> 40:14.412
Keep going! Keep going…

40:15.121 --> 40:16.705
[groaning]

40:18.165 --> 40:20.543
[Mi-jin] No! No, stop it!

40:21.293 --> 40:23.212
No! Wait!

40:23.838 --> 40:26.465
-I'm sorry!
-[groaning]

40:27.800 --> 40:29.427
[screams]

40:37.476 --> 40:38.477
Push!

40:38.561 --> 40:39.812
[grunting]

40:41.939 --> 40:43.190
[Su-hyeok] Push!

40:43.691 --> 40:45.985
-[all grunting]
-[growling]

40:49.864 --> 40:50.990
Push!

40:51.073 --> 40:52.783
[all grunting]

40:57.413 --> 40:59.165
-[all grunting]
-[growling]

40:59.248 --> 41:00.416
Damn it!

41:01.834 --> 41:02.960
[grunts]

41:10.342 --> 41:15.014
[bones crunching]

41:18.559 --> 41:20.311
[whimpers]

41:23.814 --> 41:24.815
[growls]

41:27.109 --> 41:28.402
[growls]

41:30.237 --> 41:31.363
[growls]

41:40.706 --> 41:43.083
HYOSAN

41:43.167 --> 41:44.627
[NIS agent] Each of those red dots

41:44.710 --> 41:47.671
is the location
of a random cell phone in Hyosan.

41:50.174 --> 41:54.553
At first, they begin with erratic movement
and that gives us nothing to analyze.

41:56.639 --> 41:59.266
But slowly, they move collectively.

42:01.101 --> 42:04.438
If you look at them as a whole,
they're traveling outward.

42:06.524 --> 42:09.610
Because there is nobody left
in the city to eat.

42:10.152 --> 42:13.197
They're slowly beginning
to increase their territory.

42:13.280 --> 42:16.242
Consider them like a dangerous animal
in the mountains

42:16.325 --> 42:19.370
entering civilization
when they run out of food.

42:20.538 --> 42:22.122
Let's just cut to the chase.

42:23.791 --> 42:25.376
You predicted a spread, right?

42:26.043 --> 42:28.546
That's why you proposed
expanding martial law

42:28.629 --> 42:30.381
to the NSC when Yangdong's gone.

42:35.844 --> 42:37.888
So it isn't entirely precise.

42:38.764 --> 42:39.640
But look.

42:40.808 --> 42:44.436
In one week, it reaches Seongnam,
Hanam, Gwacheon, Anyang,

42:44.520 --> 42:45.354
and Gwangmyeong.

42:48.107 --> 42:50.859
Coming right after, the city of Seoul.

42:50.943 --> 42:53.070
Seems a bit of a stretch, if you ask me.

42:53.153 --> 42:54.613
Just one person.

42:55.197 --> 42:56.907
It's a simulation of what will happen

42:56.991 --> 42:59.493
if just one infected person
gets out of Hyosan.

43:04.957 --> 43:06.375
[NIS agent] That's what will happen.

43:11.589 --> 43:13.757
[researcher] Her heart rate
is reaching 250.

43:13.841 --> 43:15.384
[Eun-ji whimpers]

43:15.467 --> 43:17.303
Abnormal heart rate detected!

43:18.095 --> 43:19.638
[Eun-ji grunts]

43:21.890 --> 43:23.892
[alarm wailing]

43:29.481 --> 43:34.320
I'M HUNGRY

43:36.113 --> 43:39.283
[screaming]

43:40.784 --> 43:44.079
[Seon-moo] Tell Tactics to come up
with a strategy to bomb Hyosan.

43:45.748 --> 43:47.082
To bomb the city, sir?

43:48.876 --> 43:50.711
Do you really plan to blow up Hyosan?

43:51.879 --> 43:54.089
Hyosan may fall, but Korea will remain.

43:54.923 --> 43:56.467
Act like a damn soldier.

43:56.550 --> 43:57.426
[soldier] We can't.

43:57.509 --> 43:59.261
The infected are one thing,

43:59.345 --> 44:01.472
but what about the civilians
that we haven't rescued?

44:01.555 --> 44:03.807
Don't think about the ones
we have to kill.

44:04.308 --> 44:06.393
The ones we will save
will justify everything.

44:14.860 --> 44:15.944
[grunts]

44:17.446 --> 44:20.783
WARNING: NO TRESPASSING
PRIVATE PROPERTY OWNED BY THE SCHOOL

44:23.327 --> 44:24.953
[exhales deeply]

44:35.464 --> 44:37.925
[snarling]

44:50.813 --> 44:52.815
[suspenseful music]

44:56.235 --> 44:57.569
[Dae-su] Just a little bit more!

44:58.779 --> 45:00.280
Untie it! Untie it!

45:05.160 --> 45:06.537
[Dae-su] It's untied! Push!

45:06.620 --> 45:08.372
-Push!
-[grunts]

45:12.668 --> 45:14.545
[thumping]

45:19.842 --> 45:20.926
The door won't open!

45:21.009 --> 45:21.844
Fuck.

45:21.927 --> 45:23.053
What are you talking about?

45:23.137 --> 45:24.346
The door won't open!

45:26.598 --> 45:29.184
-[Su-hyeok grunting]
-[thumping]

45:29.268 --> 45:31.979
[groaning]

45:43.198 --> 45:44.199
[Wu-jin] Ha-ri!
[grunts]

45:51.123 --> 45:54.084
[grunting]
Fuckers! Get lost! Get out!

45:54.168 --> 45:56.211
Let go! Damn it!

45:56.295 --> 45:57.921
[yelling]

46:08.390 --> 46:09.391
[grunts]

46:18.901 --> 46:20.152
[growling]

46:27.659 --> 46:28.744
[groans]

46:41.423 --> 46:43.425
[suspenseful music]

46:51.683 --> 46:52.893
Come on. Hurry up already!

46:53.685 --> 46:56.396
It won't open.
It's locked from the outside.

46:59.691 --> 47:00.692
Shit.

47:09.034 --> 47:10.953
[thumping]

47:11.036 --> 47:12.746
[snarling]

47:32.224 --> 47:34.226
-[suspenseful music]
-[thumping]

47:47.864 --> 47:49.283
Dad, you…
[whimpers]

48:07.301 --> 48:09.303
[closing theme music]

51:52.150 --> 51:56.238
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS SHOW ARE FICTIONAL.
